      "url": "https://www.tiktok.com/@recipeincaption/video/7672481765495180552",
      "caption": "Viral Dumpling Lasagna 🥟🔥 For ALL of you asking about the app I made, just search “Osta” on the app or play store. It is free & makes cooking social media recipes way easier 🙏 Homemade dumplings meet homemade lasagna 🤝… dare I say easier, quicker, and better than both? 👀 Ingredients: -1 lb (450 g) ground chicken or pork -1/2 cup green onions, chopped -6 garlic cloves, minced -3 tbsp soy sauce -1 tbsp rice vinegar -1 tbsp toasted sesame oil -2 tbsp chili crunch -1 tbsp fresh ginger, grated -1 tbsp oyster sauce -18 to 24 wonton or dumpling wrappers -2 tbsp chicken stock (or water) For Garnish: -Soy sauce -Chili crunch -Green onions, sliced -Sesame seeds Instructions: 1. In a bowl, combine the ground chicken or pork with the green onions, garlic, soy sauce, rice vinegar, sesame oil, Chili Crunch, ginger, and oyster sauce. Mix with your hands until just combined. 2. Set up a steamer over a pot of gently boiling water. If you don’t have a steamer, simply place a heat-safe rack or trivet inside a large pot instead. Make sure your baking dish fits comfortably inside & the lid can fully close (I used an 8×8-inch dish). Keep the water level below the baking dish. 3. Briefly dip each wrapper in water for just 1–2 secs, then arrange a layer across the bottom of your dish. I used 6 wrappers per layer. Overlap them as needed to completely cover the bottom… the overlap actually helps everything hold together. 4. Spread a thin layer of the meat mixture over the wrappers. Repeat with wrappers and meat until everything is used. I made 4 layers, but work with whatever fits your dish. Finish with a final layer of wrappers, then pour the chicken stock evenly over top. 5. Carefully place the dish into your steamer, cover, & steam for 20–22 mins, keeping the water at a gentle boil. Remove once the meat is cooked through & the top is glossy. 6. Finish with a drizzle of soy sauce, plenty of chili crunch, sliced green onions, and sesame seeds. Slice it up like lasagna and enjoy this new family favorite! #dinner #recipe #tiktokrecipe #dinnerideas ",
